					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "AquaThingus\nAquaThingus\n\nIn this example we're making a symmetrical visual with a liquid esthetic.\nYou'll learn about converting colors to textures, using Fractal Noise and UV Offset.\n\nThe patch operates in three parts: first we use fractal noise to create a wave shape.\nNext we use colors, the Texture from Data node and the Slide node to create a moving gradient.\nFinally we apply the color and offset the texture."
					}
				},
