			"76": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "OFFSET TO GREATNESS\n\nFirst we multiply the wavy texture with the moving gradient.\nThe white parts of the waves receive the gradient, the black parts stay black.\n\nNext we use UV Offset to offset the colored waves by the back and white waves, this is the liquid look we want.\nMake sure to play around with the multiplier and gain parameters!\n\nNext we use Auto Mask to get rid of the black in the texture.\nThis works to our advantage when we move on to the feedback loop, creating a softer \"trail-ish\" image.\nFinally we add black back in and we are all set and done."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 606.41729736328125,
					"width": 1493.89404296875,
					"x": 1542.698486328125,
